//! VEdit's C ABI: the Rust service layer behind one generated header.
//!
//! The Qt product owns the UI (window, panels, rendering, input) and KTextEditor
//! owns the editing kernel; everything that is not UI — the project model and
//! `.f` expansion, the Verible client, SLANG deep lint, FIM, the search index,
//! the VCS backend and the settings store — lives here (C1, C4). The Qt side must
//! not grow a second implementation of any of them.
//!
//! # Shape (C2)
//!
//! * C ABI, in-process, header generated by cbindgen ([`include/vd_ffi.h`]);
//! * opaque handles and POD structs only — the header never contains a Rust type;
//! * **no blocking**: every service entry returns a `u64` job id immediately and
//!   the caller polls for the typed result, so no call on the UI thread waits for
//!   a file system, a subprocess or a socket. One job = one worker thread; the
//!   registry lives in [`service`];
//! * no per-keystroke cross-boundary call: jobs are request-scoped, not
//!   character-scoped (FIM is the one keystroke-adjacent service and it is off by
//!   default with no transport at all).
//!
//! # The seven services
//!
//! | service | module | backend |
//! | --- | --- | --- |
//! | project model + `.f` | [`project`] | `vd-config` |
//! | Verible LSP | [`lsp`] | `vd-lsp` |
//! | SLANG deep lint | [`deeplint`] | `vd-deeplint` |
//! | FIM completion | [`fim`] | `vd-fim` |
//! | search index | [`search`] | `vd-search` |
//! | VCS backend | [`vcs`] | `vd-vcs` |
//! | settings storage | [`settings`] | `vd-settings` |
//!
//! # unsafe (AC-0.4)
//!
//! This is the only crate that may contain `unsafe` (C3). It deliberately does
//! not inherit the workspace lint table; it repeats every workspace lint at the
//! same level except `unsafe_code`, which it sets to `allow`. Every other crate
//! is unchanged and still `forbid(unsafe_code)`.
//!
//! # Header generation
//!
//! `build.rs` runs cbindgen over this crate and writes `include/vd_ffi.h`. A
//! change to an export or a POD field therefore changes the header on the next
//! build, and the C++ side stops compiling until it is updated — which is what
//! the ABI falsification test relies on.
// The C-side error type is a fixed 256-byte message array (C2: no Rust type in
// the header), so every internal `Result<_, VdError>` is legitimately ~260 bytes
// and moving the message into a Box would only add an allocation before the copy
// into that array.
#![allow(clippy::result_large_err)]

pub mod capi;
pub mod deeplint;
pub mod fim;
pub mod lsp;
pub mod project;
pub mod search;
pub mod service;
pub mod settings;
pub mod vcs;

/// Version of the C ABI. Bumped when an existing signature changes meaning.
pub const VD_ABI_VERSION: u32 = 1;
